  "slug": "syncora-accountant-client-review",
  "title": "Preparing a Client Voucher Review With Syncora",
  "description": "Agree on a period and spot-check a small sample of vouchers before reviewing synced records with a client.",
  "category": "Accountant and team workflows",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Agree on the company and period",
      "body": "Confirm the client company name and reporting dates before the meeting. Ask for a sync close to the review time and note when it completes. A period boundary or year selection can otherwise make two reviewers see different results."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Select a small transaction sample",
      "body": "Choose a few records with different purposes, such as a sale, receipt and credit note, if they exist for that client. Compare each type, number, date and amount against TallyPrime. Record a mismatch separately from your review conclusions."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Close with specific follow-ups",
      "body": "Summarize the unresolved vouchers, the responsible person and the information still needed. Avoid sending a full ledger when a single redacted reference will do. Recheck the selected entries after any correction and subsequent sync."
    }
  ],
  "relatedPaths": [
    "/for-accountants",
    "/guides/tally-ledger-on-mobile"
  ]
}
